Final Java project: a **grade calculator** that turns a score into a letter grade using a method.

Write a reusable method `gradeOf` that returns a `String`:

```java
static String gradeOf(int score) {
    if (score >= 90) return "A";
    if (score >= 80) return "B";
    if (score >= 70) return "C";
    if (score >= 60) return "D";
    return "F";
}
```

Note the early-return pattern — each `return` exits immediately, so you don't need `else`.

To read input from the user, use `Scanner` from `java.util`:

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
System.out.print("Enter score: ");
int score = scanner.nextInt();
```

Combine it all in main:

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    static String gradeOf(int score) {
        if (score >= 90) return "A";
        if (score >= 80) return "B";
        if (score >= 70) return "C";
        if (score >= 60) return "D";
        return "F";
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter score: ");
        int score = scanner.nextInt();
        System.out.println("Grade: " + gradeOf(score));
    }
}
```

